Step 3: Send Token from Frontend to API

Use Postman, cURL, or a frontend app to send a request.

A. Test with cURL

curl -X GET "http://localhost:5000/user/profile" \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN"

✅ Replace YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN with the actual token.

B. Test with Postman

1. Open Postman


2. Set Method to GET → Enter URL: http://localhost:5000/user/profile


3. Go to Authorization tab → Choose Bearer Token


4. Paste the token in the token field


5. Send Request



✅ If successful, the response should contain the User ID and Email.


