Step 5: Manually Inspect Token Claims

If User.Identity.IsAuthenticated is false, manually decode the token:

using System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt;

var handler = new JwtSecurityTokenHandler();
var jwtToken = handler.ReadJwtToken("YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN");

Console.WriteLine($"Issuer: {jwtToken.Issuer}");
Console.WriteLine($"Audience: {jwtToken.Audiences.FirstOrDefault()}");
Console.WriteLine($"Claims: {string.Join(", ", jwtToken.Claims.Select(c => $"{c.Type}: {c.Value}"))}");

✅ Check if:

aud (Audience) matches your API Client ID

iss (Issuer) matches your B2C Tenant URL

Claims contain email, name, etc.



---

Step 6: Fix Common Issues

❌ Getting 401 Unauthorized?

Ensure the API Client ID in ValidAudience matches the aud claim in the token.

Ensure the token is actually being sent in requests (Check logs).


❌ CORS issues?

If calling from frontend, make sure CORS is enabled in API:

builder.Services.AddCors(options =>
{
    options.AddPolicy("AllowAll", policy =>
        policy.AllowAnyOrigin()
              .AllowAnyMethod()
              .AllowAnyHeader());
});

app.UseCors("AllowAll");



